# A CANDIDATE: A PARK PACED BY THE HOST (the operator's "C", 2026-11-26: the ZFS ARC
# counted by the server, staged 0032, and the copy paced by the engine).
# engine-fade.series, the LIVE engine aea955022a8f, line for line, then:
#   0033  EVERY park copies its weights to host memory in 256 MiB pieces and waits
#         before each, at most GGML_SYCL_PARK_HOST_WAIT_MS, while MemAvailable is under
#         the reserve plus the piece; at that bound the weights stay on the device. The
#         reserve: GGML_SYCL_PARK_HOST_RESERVE=<bytes> in a model's env, 2 GiB unset or 0
#         - no unpaced park, since 0032 counts the ARC for every park (architecture,
#         2026-11-27). The reserve must not be above zfs_arc_sys_free; this engine goes
#         live BEFORE the server's 0032.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-pace.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ANOTHER ENGINE: a build and every gate again. Every park is paced; no model's
# answer can move.
